{
  "case_id": "2010-09-10245",
  "document_hash": "2f7b7ca9a105c4f4840a958c1b566a8519b9aede67362c32d5d507c485880716",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Frank W. Heft, Jr., Esq.",
      "case_id": "2010-09-10245",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f7b7ca9a105c4f4840a958c1b566a8519b9aede67362c32d5d507c485880716",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f7b7ca9a105-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "William Freeman's plea agreement, his presentence report, and the sentencing record all show that his term of imprisonment was based on a crack cocaine guideline that was retroactively lowered by the United States Sentencing Commission."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2010-09-10245",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f7b7ca9a105c4f4840a958c1b566a8519b9aede67362c32d5d507c485880716",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f7b7ca9a105-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: If -- if we issue an opinion and we analyze the statute's language, the statute's purpose, and the statute's legislative history, would the opinion, the judgment be based on each of those or -- or not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Solicitor General",
      "case_id": "2010-09-10245",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f7b7ca9a105c4f4840a958c1b566a8519b9aede67362c32d5d507c485880716",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f7b7ca9a105-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Solicitor General claims that since every plea negotiation has to start with the guideline calculation as a starting point for departure and/or consideration by the judge under 6B1, that every C plea agreement would be considered based on."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-09-10245",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f7b7ca9a105c4f4840a958c1b566a8519b9aede67362c32d5d507c485880716",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f7b7ca9a105-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Incidentally, and it sort of bears upon this discussion, are the guidelines mandatory when they are applied in approving a plea agreement? In other words, does Booker/Fanfan not apply to the application of the guidelines when a judge is -\u00ad is approving a plea agreement? Do you think the guidelines are mandatory in that situation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent (Curtis E. Gannon)",
      "case_id": "2010-09-10245",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f7b7ca9a105c4f4840a958c1b566a8519b9aede67362c32d5d507c485880716",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f7b7ca9a105-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When a criminal defendant and the government agree to a specific sentence and that agreement is binding on the sentencing judge by virtue of Rule 11(c)(1)(C), the resulting sentence is based on the parties' agreement. It is not based on the advisory guideline range that would otherwise have been used at sentencing, even if the sentence corresponds to that range."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent (Curtis E. Gannon)",
      "case_id": "2010-09-10245",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f7b7ca9a105c4f4840a958c1b566a8519b9aede67362c32d5d507c485880716",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f7b7ca9a105-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The agreement expressly contemplates that the judge needs to determine the applicable guideline range for purposes of determining what the fine will be."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2010-09-10245",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f7b7ca9a105c4f4840a958c1b566a8519b9aede67362c32d5d507c485880716",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f7b7ca9a105-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If I could just, while I've got you, jump to this question of what happens on remand if you lose the case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-09-10245",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f7b7ca9a105c4f4840a958c1b566a8519b9aede67362c32d5d507c485880716",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f7b7ca9a105-0001-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the policy statement, 1B1.10, which the Court last term in Dillon held is binding and controls what needs to be done during the sentence reduction proceeding. And it specifically refers to the guideline provisions that were applied when the defendant was sentenced."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gannon (Government)",
      "case_id": "2010-09-10245",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f7b7ca9a105c4f4840a958c1b566a8519b9aede67362c32d5d507c485880716",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f7b7ca9a105-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GANNON: Well, I -- I understand the point that the analysis has certainly changed since Booker, but it is still the case that the defendant can appeal an error in application of the guidelines after Booker."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gannon (Government)",
      "case_id": "2010-09-10245",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f7b7ca9a105c4f4840a958c1b566a8519b9aede67362c32d5d507c485880716",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f7b7ca9a105-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GANNON: Well, I think in the context of an actual specific sentence plea agreement, that is the one that we think is off the table, because that is what is going to control the sentence. And some type C plea agreements affirmatively contemplate application of the guidelines, as this one does with respect to the fine."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2010-09-10245",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f7b7ca9a105c4f4840a958c1b566a8519b9aede67362c32d5d507c485880716",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f7b7ca9a105-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: How do you want us to take this, pre-Booker or post-Booker?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2010-09-10245",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2f7b7ca9a105c4f4840a958c1b566a8519b9aede67362c32d5d507c485880716",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2f7b7ca9a105-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: I want an answer to my hypothetical, because I am trying to figure out how to think about it, and you will help me if you answer my hypothetical."
    },
    {
